Produce four things:

1. findings_summary — 3 to 5 sentences on what these sources collectively establish.
   State only what the sources support. If they disagree, say they disagree.

2. unknown_entities — specific named things (people, products, standards, papers,
   companies, technical terms, protocols) that appear in these sources, matter to
   the question, and are NOT explained by the sources themselves. These become
   targeted follow-up searches. Empty list if none. Do not list things you
   personally happen to know about — list things the SOURCES leave unexplained.

3. gaps — sub-questions the original question requires an answer to, that these
   sources do not answer. Phrase each as a researchable question. Be specific:
   "no primary-source data on failure rates after 2023" beats "needs more detail".

4. sufficient — true only if a careful analyst could write a well-supported,
   properly caveated answer to the research question from these sources alone.
   Default to false. Bias toward more research; a false negative costs one round,
   a false positive costs the whole report.

Reply with ONLY this JSON object:
{
